WEBVTT

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:06.519
The Matter fog is getting thicker.

00:00:07.102 --> 00:00:09.730
It's getting warmer since the sun came up.

00:00:10.773 --> 00:00:11.899
Matter fog?

00:00:11.982 --> 00:00:13.609
This mist.

00:00:14.193 --> 00:00:18.280
For the Matter to maintain its tissue,
it absorbs the river water,

00:00:18.572 --> 00:00:20.533
then metabolizes and excretes it.

00:00:22.618 --> 00:00:24.286
It's no ordinary mist.

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:27.831
It makes it hard to see
and hinders radio signals.

00:00:28.165 --> 00:00:30.709
Carbon nanostructure particles in it cause

00:00:31.085 --> 00:00:32.753
electromagnetic disturbance.

00:00:33.128 --> 00:00:35.256
Don't worry. We'll protect you.

00:00:36.507 --> 00:00:37.633
Thank you.

00:00:37.716 --> 00:00:39.927
You don't need to be so polite to me.

00:00:40.052 --> 00:00:41.804
Kazuki! Activity level!

00:00:42.304 --> 00:00:43.138
Yes, sir!

00:00:43.722 --> 00:00:47.017
But, we just entered the Area.

00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:50.521
There's red Matter activity!

00:00:52.398 --> 00:00:53.357
Even here?

00:00:54.775 --> 00:00:55.651
What is that?

00:00:58.112 --> 00:00:59.280
Divers?

00:01:00.239 --> 00:01:01.198
Stay alert!

00:01:04.076 --> 00:01:05.369
-Hey!
-They're alive!

00:01:11.417 --> 00:01:12.584
Are you all right?

00:01:13.877 --> 00:01:15.379
-What?
-What is that?

00:01:26.765 --> 00:01:28.225
Malignant Matter!

00:01:32.771 --> 00:01:34.398
They were defeated here?

00:01:34.648 --> 00:01:35.649
Kazuki! Evidence!

00:01:35.733 --> 00:01:36.942
Oh, right!

00:01:37.901 --> 00:01:38.736
Alpha Two zeta!

00:01:38.819 --> 00:01:40.988
It's already time to use this guy?

00:01:42.072 --> 00:01:43.490
What joke is this?

00:01:52.333 --> 00:01:53.334
It's not working!

00:01:56.545 --> 00:01:57.379
No way!

00:01:59.214 --> 00:02:01.550
A carbon reaction
so near the entrance?

00:02:02.509 --> 00:02:04.053
Advising Delta Two Theta!

00:02:04.136 --> 00:02:06.263
Only if it's Alpha Two derived!

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:15.564
Nice!

00:02:15.814 --> 00:02:17.775
Shino! Sever the roots!

00:02:31.455 --> 00:02:32.706
It crystallized.

00:04:06.008 --> 00:04:09.303
<i>Class Delta? But we're still in Area One!</i>

00:04:09.386 --> 00:04:13.474
That carbon-hardened stuff is never here.
It's always farther in!

00:04:13.682 --> 00:04:15.976
We can't rely on our coil guns now.

00:04:16.059 --> 00:04:18.395
Surprises right from the start.

00:04:19.605 --> 00:04:21.106
From the recent activity?

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:22.941
I'm pretty sure.

00:04:26.028 --> 00:04:26.862
Are you awake?

00:04:27.446 --> 00:04:30.491
I bet the change has affected
the entire Area.

00:04:31.116 --> 00:04:32.743
This doesn't bode well.

00:04:34.328 --> 00:04:36.079
I'm sorry!

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:37.956
Don't worry about it.

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:40.584
I was the same my first time.

00:04:44.129 --> 00:04:44.963
Are you okay?

00:04:45.422 --> 00:04:46.256
Yeah.

00:04:47.758 --> 00:04:51.261
First, we will use
the Matter Cleaving Gate at K1,

00:04:51.345 --> 00:04:55.849
between Areas One and Two.
That will wipe out everything downstream,

00:04:56.725 --> 00:05:00.312
temporarily stop Matter activity
in the immediate area,

00:05:00.479 --> 00:05:02.147
and secure the camp.

00:05:03.148 --> 00:05:06.318
The teams will split up
as we head toward K1.

00:05:07.069 --> 00:05:10.572
Seri and Misawa's team will escort
Tachibana and Kanzaki

00:05:11.156 --> 00:05:13.992
through the less contaminated
research facility.

00:05:14.827 --> 00:05:18.747
Sagami and Minase's team
will move upriver to distract the Matter.

00:05:19.122 --> 00:05:21.250
You'll swap roles in the next Area.

00:05:21.834 --> 00:05:23.877
Shiraishi is with Seri and Misawa.

00:05:24.253 --> 00:05:26.463
and I'll go with Sagami and Minase.

00:05:26.547 --> 00:05:28.131
We'll judge the competition.

00:05:28.423 --> 00:05:30.884
This is so unfair.

00:05:30.968 --> 00:05:33.345
How's it not fair?
We're taking turns.

00:05:33.595 --> 00:05:35.973
We'll evaluate both offense and defense.

00:05:36.139 --> 00:05:39.184
And we'll be sharing
the mission log with everyone.

00:05:39.518 --> 00:05:42.187
-What?
-They will know everything we do.

00:05:42.271 --> 00:05:43.146
And Evidence?

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:46.733
We're looking for any
regularity in the transformation.

00:05:47.985 --> 00:05:49.570
What is Evidence?

00:05:49.653 --> 00:05:54.783
Evidence is a database that compiles
the combat experience from all the Divers.

00:05:55.158 --> 00:05:58.829
The most effective laser wavelength
and vial cartridge compound

00:05:58.912 --> 00:06:01.373
depends on the type of Matter.

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:04.376
A vial cartridge is a bullet

00:06:04.835 --> 00:06:08.589
that contains a drug
to inhibit Matter activity.

00:06:14.845 --> 00:06:18.849
<i>If the Malignant Matter is going to</i>
<i>flow into the Sea of Japan,</i>

00:06:19.433 --> 00:06:22.185
It's better to destroy it before it does.

00:06:22.769 --> 00:06:25.522
Stopping the region's
hydroelectric generators

00:06:25.606 --> 00:06:27.024
isn't ideal, either.

00:06:27.608 --> 00:06:29.610
Thank you for your opinions.

00:06:30.027 --> 00:06:33.697
I'd like to consult
the Control Agency of Artificial Creatures

00:06:33.989 --> 00:06:36.408
before deciding what to do.

00:06:36.491 --> 00:06:39.953
We don't want just words. We need action!

00:06:40.037 --> 00:06:41.038
May I speak?

00:06:41.788 --> 00:06:45.334
Total destruction
of the Malignant Matter Area

00:06:45.417 --> 00:06:50.172
is the same as abandoning
our country's accumulated knowledge

00:06:50.255 --> 00:06:52.341
in artificial organism research.

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:53.884
Slides.

00:06:56.053 --> 00:07:01.224
<i>I have already explained several times</i>
<i>that the mere presence of the Matter</i>

00:07:01.308 --> 00:07:04.061
<i>gives us an advantage</i>
<i>over other countries.</i>

00:07:04.937 --> 00:07:07.773
<i>The future of Japan's</i>
<i>science and technology,</i>

00:07:07.856 --> 00:07:10.400
<i>as well as our economy and manufacturing,</i>

00:07:10.484 --> 00:07:12.861
<i>will rest on cell assembler technology</i>

00:07:12.945 --> 00:07:14.738
<i>and carbon nanostructures.</i>

00:07:15.197 --> 00:07:17.824
<i>I trust all</i>
<i>the esteemed individuals here</i>

00:07:17.908 --> 00:07:20.285
<i>understand just</i>
<i>how damaging it would be</i>

00:07:20.494 --> 00:07:23.163
<i>to the country if we were to sacrifice</i>

00:07:23.705 --> 00:07:25.499
this precious legacy,

00:07:25.582 --> 00:07:28.961
which is the foundation of our future.

00:07:29.044 --> 00:07:30.754
Is the safety of our citizens

00:07:30.837 --> 00:07:33.382
not more important than money?

00:07:33.757 --> 00:07:35.050
Let me point out

00:07:35.133 --> 00:07:37.803
if the Matter
is not eliminated all at once,

00:07:38.011 --> 00:07:41.098
it's possible we
will only aggravate the situation.

00:07:41.515 --> 00:07:43.141
Who will own that disaster?

00:07:45.811 --> 00:07:48.814
Would you still call for flames and fire

00:07:49.272 --> 00:07:51.900
if this were on the Tonegawa River?

00:07:53.443 --> 00:07:56.655
Professor Isazu won't be coming here.

00:07:57.239 --> 00:07:58.782
Tell me about Aiko Tachibana.

00:07:59.366 --> 00:08:00.701
Arrangements are made

00:08:00.784 --> 00:08:04.663
for dispatching Ozanami's squad
into the Area.

00:08:05.455 --> 00:08:07.416
The problem is Yuya Kanzaki.

00:08:07.499 --> 00:08:09.084
I wonder who he is.

00:08:09.167 --> 00:08:12.170
He's so bold,
I thought I could find...

00:08:12.254 --> 00:08:13.505
May I?

00:08:14.006 --> 00:08:15.465
Hey! I was saving that!

00:08:21.346 --> 00:08:24.933
So, you know how to drive one of those.

00:08:25.267 --> 00:08:26.101
Yes.

00:08:26.393 --> 00:08:27.394
Hey...

00:08:27.477 --> 00:08:28.311
What?

00:08:28.937 --> 00:08:32.357
I didn't realize
how tough it was being a Diver.

00:08:33.775 --> 00:08:35.736
This is nothing.

00:08:36.236 --> 00:08:38.530
The job ends when we secure our target

00:08:38.613 --> 00:08:41.783
and return it to the client undamaged.

00:08:42.325 --> 00:08:45.537
But this time
we have to deliver you undamaged,

00:08:46.038 --> 00:08:47.748
so it's a pretty weird job.

00:08:48.915 --> 00:08:51.251
-I'm sorry.
-Why are you apologizing?

00:08:52.044 --> 00:08:54.546
Thanks to you, I'm getting a huge salary.

00:08:54.963 --> 00:08:57.507
Just shut up and let us work.

00:09:03.555 --> 00:09:06.641
The fog will block
radio transmissions from here on.

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:10.395
Switch from GPS navigation
to autonomous geopositioning.

00:09:11.021 --> 00:09:14.316
Switch from close-range comms
to optical as well.

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:16.485
I wish everyone the best!

00:09:17.027 --> 00:09:17.944
-Wilco!
-Wilco!

00:09:21.156 --> 00:09:22.240
Latent activity!

00:09:22.824 --> 00:09:24.951
Activity level increasing, from one

00:09:25.535 --> 00:09:26.953
<i>two, three.</i>

00:09:27.746 --> 00:09:28.830
Identified!

00:09:29.289 --> 00:09:31.833
Evidence updated
with previous contact data!

00:09:31.917 --> 00:09:34.753
All right. Let's have some fun!

00:09:44.513 --> 00:09:45.514
Yes!

00:09:46.765 --> 00:09:49.351
This groggy Matter is no match for us!

00:09:49.434 --> 00:09:51.478
Make sure you're wide awake, too!

00:09:53.313 --> 00:09:55.065
Looks like we woke up a mob.

00:10:04.241 --> 00:10:08.578
We will play with you, so leave
the young man and woman alone!

00:10:10.622 --> 00:10:11.456
What?

00:10:13.083 --> 00:10:14.417
What is going on?

00:10:14.501 --> 00:10:16.586
We got through here a few days ago.

00:10:17.337 --> 00:10:19.923
We'll have to go
down to the river, too.

00:10:20.006 --> 00:10:21.341
How lucky are we?

00:10:22.717 --> 00:10:25.095
It means we can score some points.

00:10:36.314 --> 00:10:37.941
This is more like it!

00:10:40.318 --> 00:10:42.320
Don't go nuts.
You'll get surrounded.

00:10:42.904 --> 00:10:44.072
I know!

00:10:50.662 --> 00:10:52.414
New growth from another trunk!

00:10:52.497 --> 00:10:54.332
Evidence! Bravo Six!

00:11:00.547 --> 00:11:01.464
No good!

00:11:02.173 --> 00:11:03.466
Switch to Echo Three!

00:11:11.099 --> 00:11:12.100
Thanks!

00:11:13.643 --> 00:11:16.897
It's resistant to both chemical
and physical attacks.

00:11:17.898 --> 00:11:20.734
Our distance from Primary Point
doesn't seem to matter.

00:11:21.401 --> 00:11:22.235
Tachibana!

00:11:25.447 --> 00:11:26.281
Four o'clock!

00:11:34.122 --> 00:11:35.248
What?

00:11:37.918 --> 00:11:39.419
Why are you down here?

00:11:39.836 --> 00:11:43.924
The tunnel was plugged with Matter!
Are you trying to steal my kills?

00:11:44.132 --> 00:11:45.675
We saved your ass!

00:11:45.759 --> 00:11:48.887
New enemy! Evidence! Advising Echo Nine!

00:11:48.970 --> 00:11:50.513
You're the slow ones!

00:11:50.764 --> 00:11:52.140
This is our section!

00:11:52.265 --> 00:11:55.936
Another new enemy! Advising Delta Seven!

00:12:03.193 --> 00:12:05.111
<i>It's been two years, you know,</i>

00:12:05.904 --> 00:12:09.449
<i>since he joined us, took over my research,</i>

00:12:10.075 --> 00:12:12.577
<i>and developed Cell Assembler Two.</i>

00:12:14.329 --> 00:12:16.456
If Toshi were alive,

00:12:17.082 --> 00:12:19.668
we may have been able to take care of this

00:12:20.335 --> 00:12:22.087
and develop further, as well.

00:12:22.712 --> 00:12:25.590
We'll make the most of
what Yura left behind.

00:12:34.599 --> 00:12:35.433
Thank you

00:12:35.767 --> 00:12:39.062
for letting me use his
his startup budget freely.

00:12:41.231 --> 00:12:43.733
I will repay you someday, I swear.

00:12:50.407 --> 00:12:51.491
Kurose!

00:12:52.867 --> 00:12:54.327
It's been a while.

00:12:54.661 --> 00:12:56.162
Hey, Isazu!

00:12:56.621 --> 00:12:58.456
Busy with research as always?

00:12:59.124 --> 00:13:00.750
My position keeps me busy.

00:13:02.294 --> 00:13:03.461
Visiting Dr. Kiryu?

00:13:03.586 --> 00:13:04.421
Yes.

00:13:04.629 --> 00:13:06.047
You seem pretty busy.

00:13:06.631 --> 00:13:08.091
You, too.

00:13:08.299 --> 00:13:11.052
I heard you and Nanbara
are up to something.

00:13:11.886 --> 00:13:14.305
Just the university lab reunion.

00:13:14.889 --> 00:13:15.724
See you there?

00:13:16.057 --> 00:13:17.517
Sounds nice.

00:13:18.059 --> 00:13:20.103
And there's things
I want to settle with you.

00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:22.188
Oh, by the way.

00:13:24.441 --> 00:13:25.400
I take it back.

00:13:25.734 --> 00:13:26.568
What?

00:13:26.943 --> 00:13:31.156
My opinion that we incinerate the Area
and clear out the Matter.

00:13:31.531 --> 00:13:33.533
Really? That's quite a change.

00:13:34.117 --> 00:13:35.744
Since Yura passed away,

00:13:36.286 --> 00:13:39.330
I doubt we'll find
the Yura Notes we all want.

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:44.169
The important things exist
only inside the Area.

00:13:44.252 --> 00:13:46.921
It's not like you
to switch sides like that.

00:13:47.797 --> 00:13:51.593
We can't make any progress
unless we accept reality, right?

00:14:08.610 --> 00:14:09.944
This was a hot spring.

00:14:10.028 --> 00:14:11.863
I want a bath!

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:16.534
Alert!

00:14:16.618 --> 00:14:18.328
Active organisms detected!

00:14:23.541 --> 00:14:26.628
Those aren't bathers, so what are they?

00:14:27.545 --> 00:14:29.422
Probably Divers that were killed here.

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:30.924
No.

00:14:31.132 --> 00:14:33.051
They're not wearing Diver Suits.

00:14:34.177 --> 00:14:36.805
Is the Matter taking the form of people?

00:14:37.722 --> 00:14:38.556
Evidence!

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:40.642
No encounter history!

00:14:40.975 --> 00:14:41.935
It's a new type?

00:14:42.519 --> 00:14:43.853
What's going on?

00:14:44.437 --> 00:14:47.607
Everyone, ready your MP Vials
and stun weapons!

00:15:09.838 --> 00:15:11.840
They're coming back in human form.

00:15:11.923 --> 00:15:13.216
What the hell?!

00:15:25.895 --> 00:15:26.729
Damn!

00:15:27.147 --> 00:15:28.189
Is this working?

00:15:28.273 --> 00:15:29.107
I don't know.

00:15:29.190 --> 00:15:31.067
We just have to open the way.

00:15:33.236 --> 00:15:36.823
Tachibana! Relax! Breathe deep and slow.

00:15:40.952 --> 00:15:44.330
Escort these two
into the commuter rail terminal!

00:15:46.249 --> 00:15:47.292
Crap!

00:15:47.375 --> 00:15:48.960
What the hell is going on?

00:15:49.377 --> 00:15:51.880
These have never been encountered before.

00:15:51.963 --> 00:15:54.215
The Matter is growing human forms?

00:15:54.424 --> 00:15:58.094
I think the Matter is
feeding off of the humans.

00:15:58.970 --> 00:16:00.638
This is no ordinary Matter.

00:16:03.016 --> 00:16:03.850
Shiraishi!

00:16:04.476 --> 00:16:05.977
Take those two to K1!

00:16:06.311 --> 00:16:07.562
Sagami, escort them!

00:16:07.645 --> 00:16:11.983
Shino, if you don't go with Shiraishi,
we can't operate the Cleaving Gate!

00:16:13.651 --> 00:16:15.487
Right. I'm counting on you!

00:16:33.546 --> 00:16:35.006
Activity level four!

00:16:35.089 --> 00:16:36.257
Seriously?

00:16:36.341 --> 00:16:38.092
How can that happen here?

00:16:38.259 --> 00:16:41.971
We can investigate later,
as long as we're still alive.

00:16:42.555 --> 00:16:43.806
I know I'll be!

00:16:49.145 --> 00:16:49.979
A flash pile!

00:16:50.647 --> 00:16:52.232
Nice! Lure them in!

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:04.994
Almost there.

00:17:05.453 --> 00:17:06.287
Okay.

00:17:08.623 --> 00:17:11.543
The Matter got over that giant dam?

00:17:12.502 --> 00:17:15.838
That thing above the dam
is the Matter Cleaving Gate,

00:17:16.297 --> 00:17:17.924
aka the Guillotine Shutter.

00:17:37.443 --> 00:17:38.403
Kanzaki!

00:17:44.784 --> 00:17:46.411
Tachibana, are you okay?

00:17:59.591 --> 00:18:02.343
-Where is the control console?
-SWS 201.

00:18:02.427 --> 00:18:05.513
-Kanzaki, can I leave her with you?
-Yes, sir!

00:18:12.020 --> 00:18:14.355
Link in via
the Diver Suit registration organism.

00:18:15.523 --> 00:18:17.233
Verify organism data.

00:18:17.984 --> 00:18:18.860
Linked.

00:18:26.784 --> 00:18:27.869
VERIFIED
ACTIVATED

00:18:29.662 --> 00:18:30.496
Nicely done.

00:18:42.425 --> 00:18:43.718
Here it comes!

00:18:44.302 --> 00:18:46.012
-Kaede!
-Time to go!

00:18:47.347 --> 00:18:48.473
<i>After going online,</i>

00:18:48.931 --> 00:18:52.060
<i>the shutter is raised</i>
<i>to its starting position.</i>

00:18:52.769 --> 00:18:55.730
Then a linear induction motor
propels it downward.

00:18:56.147 --> 00:18:58.358
<i>The moment it slices,</i>

00:18:58.524 --> 00:19:00.735
<i>it emits a massive electrical charge.</i>

00:19:05.865 --> 00:19:07.408
Diver evacuation complete.

00:19:08.368 --> 00:19:09.202
Let's do this.

00:19:12.372 --> 00:19:13.998
-Ready, go!
-Ready, go!

00:19:37.021 --> 00:19:40.274
<i>The severed Matter downriver</i>
<i>from the dam is destroyed.</i>

00:19:40.608 --> 00:19:43.611
<i>The electric charge temporarily</i>
<i>paralyzed the nearby Matter,</i>

00:19:44.028 --> 00:19:45.446
<i>ceasing all activity.</i>

00:19:46.739 --> 00:19:48.825
<i>You can rest easy to the next camp,</i>

00:19:49.534 --> 00:19:53.287
<i>at least until the active Matter</i>
<i>sprouts new branches.</i>

00:19:55.832 --> 00:19:58.584
<i>It looks like we survived this.</i>

00:20:06.300 --> 00:20:09.220
Yuzuha was a very good girl again today.

00:20:10.304 --> 00:20:12.640
I see. I'm sorry for all the trouble.

00:20:13.224 --> 00:20:14.600
No problem.

00:20:15.727 --> 00:20:18.521
I sure hope she wakes up soon.

00:20:19.772 --> 00:20:21.149
I know she will.

00:20:23.526 --> 00:20:25.319
TOYAMA YOUTH MUSIC COMPETITION

00:20:28.030 --> 00:20:28.865
Saho.

00:20:29.240 --> 00:20:30.116
Yes?

00:20:30.742 --> 00:20:31.826
It feels like...

00:20:32.952 --> 00:20:35.163
this girl is testing

00:20:36.205 --> 00:20:38.082
my true worth as a doctor.

00:20:43.045 --> 00:20:47.216
So, I have to do whatever it takes

00:20:48.801 --> 00:20:50.678
to overcome this challenge.

00:20:54.599 --> 00:20:55.850
<i>The fog has lifted.</i>

00:20:57.268 --> 00:20:58.352
<i>Ironic, isn't it?</i>

00:20:58.770 --> 00:21:01.689
<i>It's so beautiful</i>
<i>when it's dead and withered.</i>

00:21:06.110 --> 00:21:07.862
The girl appears to be okay.

00:21:08.946 --> 00:21:11.949
She doesn't look so good to me.

00:21:13.326 --> 00:21:17.163
And what about that guy?
There's something suspicious about him.

00:21:18.498 --> 00:21:20.374
We should probably go back.

00:21:20.625 --> 00:21:23.044
She doesn't look like she'll make it.

00:21:23.252 --> 00:21:25.087
What? No way!

00:21:25.171 --> 00:21:26.923
We won't get paid then!

00:21:35.723 --> 00:21:36.557
I...

00:21:39.685 --> 00:21:41.103
I will continue!

00:21:41.854 --> 00:21:44.524
My mother and brother
might still be alive.

00:21:45.107 --> 00:21:46.067
I have to go!

00:21:46.776 --> 00:21:47.693
I have to save them!

00:21:48.736 --> 00:21:51.280
Her mother and brother?

00:21:52.532 --> 00:21:53.533
Save them?

00:21:55.701 --> 00:21:56.536
Don't worry.

00:21:56.869 --> 00:21:57.703
I will...

00:21:58.663 --> 00:22:00.581
We will do whatever it takes

00:22:00.665 --> 00:22:03.376
to get you to Primary Point.

00:22:05.294 --> 00:22:06.170
I promise.

00:22:12.635 --> 00:22:14.512
<i>-Nanbara here.</i>
<i>-It's Hori!</i>

00:22:14.929 --> 00:22:17.473
<i>The Guillotine Shutter</i>
<i>at K1 was activated!</i>

00:22:18.891 --> 00:22:19.934
Are you serious?

00:22:26.065 --> 00:22:28.150
Yuya Kanzaki!

00:23:57.948 --> 00:23:59.992
Subtitles by Brian Athey
